t's part of the chow. So the best action is to play F3.\n", "output": "Evaluation: Playing F3 removes a non-essential tile and avoids disrupting potential melds in Dots (B4-B5-B6) or Characters (W6 with W5/W7 if drawn). The existing Pung of J1 and possible concealed chow in Dots are more critical for scoring.\nReason: F3 is a single honor tile with no immediate use in forming melds. Discarding it preserves key suited tiles for potential chows or pungs. The B4-B5-B6 sequence is viable for a concealed chow, and keeping all three increases chances of completing it. W9 pair remains intact for a potential pair in the final hand.\nAnswer: Play F3"}
